From 5ab3bab23412636f7e5745382c5bd0c056ccc49b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 21:38:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH net v2 3/3] bpf, sockmap: preserve self-ingress TCP sequence
 space

Sockmap stream verdict can enqueue data from the same TCP socket into
psock->ingress_msg when the program returns SK_PASS. If a later skb from
the same receive queue gets SK_DROP or SK_REDIRECT, tcp_eat_skb()
consumes TCP sequence space immediately.

This is wrong when the earlier SK_PASS data is still unread in
ingress_msg. Advancing copied_seq over the later dropped or redirected
skb first jumps over the unread SK_PASS bytes. When userspace later
reads that SK_PASS data from the sockmap ingress queue, copied_seq is
advanced again and can move beyond rcv_nxt.

The following sequence reproduces the corruption:

  1. A TCP skb reaches the sockmap verdict path.
  2. The BPF verdict returns SK_PASS, so the skb is queued on
     ingress_msg.
  3. Userspace has not read the queued SK_PASS data yet.
  4. A later skb gets SK_DROP or SK_REDIRECT.
  5. tcp_eat_skb() advances copied_seq over the later skb immediately.
  6. Userspace then reads the earlier SK_PASS data and copied_seq moves
     past rcv_nxt.

The corrupted state triggers the same receive-side warning pattern:

  TCP recvmsg seq # bug 2: copied AC41A404, seq AC41A3FA,
      rcvnxt AC41A3FB, fl 40
  WARNING: net/ipv4/tcp.c:2745 at tcp_recvmsg_locked+0x45e/0x9f0
  Call Trace:
   tcp_recvmsg_locked
   tcp_zerocopy_receive
   do_tcp_getsockopt
   tcp_getsockopt
   do_sock_getsockopt
   __sys_getsockopt

Defer TCP sequence consumption for an SK_DROP or SK_REDIRECT when there
is already self-originated SK_PASS data queued in ingress_msg. The
deferred drop length is stored on the earlier sk_msg and accounted when
that message is fully read, so copied_seq advances in receive order.
Also trim self-ingress SK_PASS data against the current copied_seq so a
socket inserted after a partial native TCP read does not deliver the
already-read prefix again.

Add regression coverage for SK_PASS followed by SK_DROP, SK_PASS
followed by SK_REDIRECT, SK_PASS after a partial native read, and
synchronize the partial-read SK_DROP test with verdict execution before
deleting the map entry.

Fixes: e5c6de5fa025 ("bpf, sockmap: Incorrectly handling copied_seq")
Link: https://lore.kernel.org/bpf/20260703140122.A07201F000E9@smtp.kernel.org/
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
